
What are Serialization and Deserialization ?
=======================================
🔹 What is Serialization?
→ Serialization means Converting an object into a transferable format like JSON or XML that can be sent or stored
Why do we need it?
To send data over the network (api response)
To save data in a file or database
To communicate between client and server
Example (Serialization)
JavaScript object:
const user = { id: 1, name: "Aziz" };
After serialization (JSON):
{"id":1,"name":"Aziz"}
👉 Object → JSON
👉 This is serialization

🔹 What is Deserialization?
Deserialization means converting the received format (JSON/XML) back into a usable object.
Example (Deserialization)
JSON received from API:
{"id":1,"name":"Aziz"}
After deserialization:
const user = { id: 1, name: "Aziz" };
👉 JSON → Object
👉 This is deserialization
Client → Server
UI sends JSON
Server converts JSON to object
👉 Deserialization
Server → Client
Server converts object to JSON
UI receives JSON
👉 Serialization

